# POP Cinemas weekly billboard

When the user shares a POP Cinemas / @cinemaspop / cinemaspop.com.do schedule (flyer, Story, screenshot, or site dump):

## Do

1. **One event per week**, not one event per film or per showtime.
2. Id pattern: `pop-cinemas-week-YYYY-MM-DD` where the date is the **Thursday** that starts the cartelera week (Thu–Wed), matching `pop-cinemas-week-2026-08-20` and `pop-cinemas-week-2026-09-11`.
3. Set `date` + `endDate` to that Thu–Wed range; `time` spans the earliest–latest published daily slot.
4. Put the full weekly list in **text**: `description` (EN/ES/FR) with title + showtime + language when known, **and** a `lineup` array of film titles (include times in the label when known). Note RD$300 and `cinemaspop.com.do` / `809-320-1400`.
5. Reuse venue `pop-cinemas-playa-dorada` (Playa Dorada Mall). Prefer the **venue place shot** as the event hero — not a schedule collage/screenshot. Wire `SEED_CREATED_AT`, opinion, `CURATED_EVENT_DETAILS` / admission `RD$300`, phone `+18093201400`, attributions.
6. If a schedule flyer/screenshot is kept for reference, mark it typography-heavy and do **not** use it as the event/home hero. Place-shot heroes may stay on the venue image path.
7. Spotlight already collapses `pop-cinemas-week-*` via `spotlightSeriesKeyFromId` — keep the dated id suffix.

## Do not

- Create separate seed events for each movie or each daily screening.
- Invent showtimes — only list times visible on the source; say “confirm on cinemaspop.com.do” when a title has no time.
- Use the weekly schedule screenshot/collage as the event hero when the films can be listed in text (`description` + `lineup`). Treat attached schedules as **source** for the text list.

## Upcoming weeks

Each new cartelera week = a **new** seed id (new Thursday). Leave prior weeks in seeds; do not overwrite an old week’s description with the new bill. Refresh the venue tip only if pricing/hours change.
